# Stranglethorn Vale, Dustwallow Marsh and the Swamp of Sorrows, Alliance ~40.5
# to ~43 (consensus visits 29 and 33-42). Flow: Theramore > one Dustwallow loop
# (Sentry Point, Swamplight Manor, North Point Tower, the Darkmist spiders,
# Mudcrush and the Shady Rest, back through Theramore, then the murlocs,
# Jarl, Mudcrush and Balos Jacken) > hearth to Theramore > ride to Ratchet
# (flight path),
# boat to Booty Bay > Stranglethorn from Booty Bay (the Bloodsail, the
# gorillas, Zanzil's village, the Crystalvein Mine and the Skullsplitters,
# then the north-west coast and the Rebel Camp, hearth to Booty Bay) >
# fly to Stormwind > Swamp of Sorrows > hearth to Stormwind > Ironforge,
# where the player flies to Thelsamar for the next guide.
#
# Deviations from the export:
# - Dustwallow Marsh's two visits (29 and 33) are merged into one loop: the
#   same hubs, walked once. Theramore's flight path and the first two
#   Missing Diplomat turn-ins come from the previous guide.
# - Stranglethorn: the far north is one loop after the jungle: The Curse of
#   the Tides (611) and Pearl Diving (705, carried from 30-40/06-badlands) on
#   the north-west coast, then Return to Corporal Kaleb (622) at the Rebel
#   Camp, closed by the hearth to Booty Bay. Raptor Mastery (196) is left
#   out: Nesingwary's camp would need a second visit for its turn-in, which
#   costs as much time as the quest saves. Goblin Sponsorship 1180-1182 is
#   left out (it starts at the Shimmering Flats). "Pretty Boy" Duncan (610)
#   is done near Booty Bay. Voodoo Dues is done on one jungle loop: Shaky is
#   visited between the gorillas and the jungle.
# - The Shimmering Flats stop (visit 36) is dropped: a long trip from
#   Stormwind. Keeping Pace and Rizzle's Schematics (1190, 1194) are done in
#   40-50/04-tanaris, which rides across the Flats; Goblin Sponsorship 1183
#   and Parts for Kravel 1112 are left out.
# - The Teldrassil trip (visit 38, Favored of Elune? 3661, a single accept)
#   and the Searing Gorge stop (visit 42, Caught! 4449) are dropped; Caught!
#   is taken by a later guide that goes to its outhouse anyway.
# - Southshore (visit 39): the previous guide already handed in its quests;
#   Down the Scarlet Path (1052) is handed in when the next guide passes
#   Southshore. Return to Milton (542, from the previous guide) is handed in
#   to Milton Sheaf on the first Stormwind stop.
# - Stormwind's two visits keep their order around the Swamp; A Meal Served
#   Cold (212) and Feast at the Blue Recluse (1271) move to the first one,
#   and Ironforge comes after the second, on the way to the Badlands.
# - Jarl Needs a Blade (1203) wants a Moonsteel Broadsword, a blacksmith's
#   craft: optional.
# - Added: Suspicious Hoofprints (1284), by the Shady Rest badge, handed in to
#   Vimes on the Theramore stop the loop already makes (James Hyal, turned
#   in the guide before, opens it).
# - Stormwind: Andromath (1477) right after Angus in the Mage Quarter, before
#   Mazen and Dellis; Brohann (1448) in the Dwarven District before Milton
#   in the Keep.
# Left out: ... and Bugs (1258), Sunken Treasure (670), Cortello's Riddle part
# 2 (625: west Dustwallow), and the Ironforge breadcrumbs Find Bingles and
# Speak with Shoni (2039, 2041): never finished on the route or dropped with
# their detour. Into The Temple of Atal'Hakkar (1475: tablets inside the
# Sunken Temple, and its opener 1469 is not on the route) and Reclaimed
# Treasures (1360: Krom's chest is inside Uldaman) are dungeon work: left out.
# Class quests: Paladins take and hand in The Tome of Nobility (1661) from
# Duthorian Rall in Stormwind; Warlocks take Summon Felsteed (4488) from
# Demisette Cloyce and hand it in at Ratchet at the end of the next guide.
# Warriors finish The Islander and The Affray (1718, 1719, Berserker Stance)
# on Fray Island on the ride to Ratchet; Klannoc's follow-up, The Windwatcher
# (1791) and the Whirlwind weapon chain with its elite, is left to the Class
# guide forever/class/warrior/whirlwind-weapon (a note at The Affray says so).
# Class training: Stormwind; Shamans at the Ironforge stop at the end.
# Riding: the Stormwind stop at about 42 is the first city after 40. Each race
# is pointed to its own riding trainer and mount vendor: Humans to Randal
# Hunter and Katie Hunter in Elwynn, Night Elves to Jartsam and Lelanai in
# Darnassus, Skyborne to Randal Hunter (no Skyborne riding trainer is known;
# their Galestriders come from Genn Fairweather on Zephras Isle), all from the
# Stormwind stop; Dwarves to Ultham Ironhorn and Veron Amberstill and Gnomes
# to Binjy and Milli Featherwhistle from the Ironforge stop. Forever may let
# any race learn from any riding trainer (unconfirmed). Every goal is
# optional (100g).
# The Bloodsail captains (608) are optional: 45-48 on decks of 42-45 pirates.
# Added: My Little Friends (93176, Forever, from 30-40/05-arathi-highlands):
# the Arbor Tarantula (data spawn 43-44,17-19) is caught on the ride to the
# Rebel Camp and the quest is handed to Amaryllis Webb on the Swamp stop, as
# the consensus does (42.9); based on data, not play (Forever above 30 is
# unchecked until 4 November).
guide forever/alliance/40-50/01-stranglethorn-vale
title Stranglethorn Vale, Dustwallow Marsh & Swamp of Sorrows
faction Alliance
levels 40-43
zone Stranglethorn Vale
next forever/alliance/40-50/02-badlands

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Theramore

step Theramore
  zone Dustwallow Marsh
  tip Morgan Stern stands near the inn; Helenia Olden, a trade supplier a few steps south, sells the spices Jarl wants.
  sethome "Theramore Isle"
  turnin 1260                         -- Morgan Stern
  accept 1204
  buy 3713 x3 npc 4897                -- Soothing Spices, for "Swamp Eye" Jarl

step Sentry Point
  tip Follow the road north-west out of Theramore to the watchtower at Sentry Point. Mudrock Burrowers roam the marsh around it.
  complete 1265 @59.9,40.9
  collect 5883 quest 1204             -- Forked Mudrock Tongue

step Archmage Tervosh
  tip Back in Theramore: Tervosh waits with Lady Jaina in the tower of Foothold Citadel.
  turnin 1265
  accept 1266

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The north

step Swamplight Manor
  tip Take the road north to the ruined manor; Jarl lives in the shack beside it and the loose dirt is at the corner of the house.
  accept 1218                         -- "Swamp Eye" Jarl
  turnin 1218                         -- with the spices from Theramore
  accept 1206
  accept 1219                         -- Loose Dirt

step Mudrock tortoises
  tip The Mudrock Tortoises and Spikeshells sun themselves on the shore north-east of the manor.
  collect 5883 quest 1204             -- Forked Mudrock Tongue

step "Stinky" Ignatz
  tip Stinky waits west of the manor, in the marsh below North Point Tower. Lead him to his Bogbean leaves and keep the swamp creatures off him.
  accept 1222
  complete 1222 @48.9,24.6

step North Point Tower
  tip Private Hendel holds the tower with a few deserters. He turns on you: beat him until he yields.
  turnin 1266                         -- Private Hendel
  accept 1324
  complete 1324

step Darkmist Cavern
  tip The Darkmist spiders nest around the cavern in the north-west of the marsh; every spider drops eyes.
  collect 5884 quest 1206             -- Unpopped Darkmist Eye

step Mudcrush Durtfeet
  tip Ride south to the giant's hut in the middle of the marsh.
  accept 1177

step The Shady Rest Inn
  tip The burned inn stands on the road west, toward the Barrens; the guard's badge lies in the ashes and the hoofprints are in the mud beside the inn.
  accept 1252 @29.8,48.2              -- Theramore Guard Badge
  accept 1284 @29.7,47.6              -- Hoofprints

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Theramore

step Theramore
  tip Follow the road east back to Theramore. Tervosh, Lady Jaina and the officers are in the tower and Foothold Citadel.
  turnin 1324                         -- Archmage Tervosh
  accept 1267                         -- Lady Jaina Proudmoore
  turnin 1267
  turnin 1219                         -- Theramore Lieutenant
  accept 1220
  turnin 1220                         -- Captain Garran Vimes
  turnin 1252
  turnin 1284
  accept 1259
  turnin 1259                         -- Adjutant Tesoran
  accept 1285
  turnin 1285                         -- Captain Garran Vimes
  accept 1286
  turnin 1222                         -- Morgan Stern

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The north again and the west

step Mirefin murlocs
  tip The Mirefin murlocs crowd the north coast past Swamplight Manor; finish the tongues on the tortoises beside them.
  collect 5847 quest 1177             -- Mirefin Head
  collect 5883 quest 1204             -- Forked Mudrock Tongue

step Swamplight Manor
  turnin 1206                         -- "Swamp Eye" Jarl
  accept 1203 optional                -- only if you carry a Moonsteel Broadsword (a blacksmith's craft)
  turnin 1203 optional

step Mudcrush Durtfeet
  turnin 1177

step Balos Jacken
  tip The deserters camp south of the road, west of Mudcrush's hut.
  turnin 1286
  accept 1287

step Theramore
  hearth "Theramore Isle"
  turnin 1287                         -- Captain Garran Vimes
  accept 1288
  turnin 1288                         -- Lady Jaina Proudmoore
  turnin 1204                         -- Morgan Stern

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Booty Bay

step The Affray
  only Warrior
  zone The Barrens
  tip On the ride north to Ratchet, Fray Island lies off the Merchant Coast south of the town: wade over the sand bar shallows. Klannoc Macleod sends four challengers and then Big Will (level 33) at you, one at a time.
  turnin 1718                             -- Klannoc Macleod
  accept 1719
  complete 1719                           -- Defeat the challengers and Big Will
  turnin 1719                             -- Klannoc Macleod: Berserker Stance
  note Klannoc offers The Windwatcher next (1791): the Whirlwind weapon chain, with an elite at the end, is in the Warrior class guide Whirlwind Weapon.

step Ratchet
  zone The Barrens
  tip Ride from Theramore west along the Dustwallow road into the Barrens and north to Ratchet on the coast. Learn the flight path from Bragok, then take the boat to Booty Bay from the dock.
  getfp "Ratchet" npc 16227           -- Bragok
  goto 63.4,38.5 "Boat to Booty Bay"

step Booty Bay
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip The Salty Sailor Tavern is the tall building over the harbour; most of the quest givers are on its floors or the docks below.
  sethome "Booty Bay"
  accept 348                          -- Fin Fizracket
  accept 595                          -- First Mate Crazz
  accept 606                          -- "Sea Wolf" MacKinley
  accept 2872                         -- for Stoley in Tanaris: keep it
  accept 600                          -- Crank Fizzlebub
  accept 621
  accept 209                          -- Kebok
  accept 2864                         -- Krazek: for Tran'rek in Tanaris, keep it
  turnin 627                          -- Krazek
  accept 622                          -- for Corporal Kaleb at the Rebel Camp, on the northern loop
  accept 617                          -- Privateer Bloads
  turnin 669                          -- Fleet Master Seahorn, top floor
  note Seahorn's next errand goes back to Arathi: skip it.
  turnin 603                          -- Catelyn the Blade
  accept 610

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The Bloodsail

step Bloodsail camp
  tip Leave town by the tunnel and follow the coast north; the letter lies in the Bloodsail camp on the beach, where "Pretty Boy" Duncan walks.
  turnin 595                          -- Bloodsail Correspondence
  accept 597
  collect 4027 quest 610              -- Catelyn's Blade

step Booty Bay
  turnin 597                          -- First Mate Crazz
  accept 599
  turnin 599                          -- Fleet Master Seahorn
  accept 604
  accept 576                          -- Dizzy One-Eye
  accept 587                          -- Deeg
  turnin 610                          -- Catelyn the Blade
  accept 611                          -- Gazban swims off the north-west coast, on the northern loop

step Bloodsail pirates
  tip Every Bloodsail drops Snuff and one of them carries Dizzy's eye; the Swashbucklers walk the shore just north of town. The charts and orders lie in the pirate camp on the Wild Shore, south of Booty Bay.
  kill 1563 quest 604                 -- Bloodsail Swashbuckler
  collect 3910 quest 587              -- Snuff
  collect 3897 quest 576              -- Dizzy's Eye
  collect 3920 quest 604              -- Bloodsail Charts
  collect 3921 quest 604              -- Bloodsail Orders

step Booty Bay
  turnin 604                          -- Fleet Master Seahorn
  accept 608
  turnin 587                          -- Deeg
  turnin 576                          -- Dizzy One-Eye

step The Bloodsail captains
  tip The captains stand on the ships anchored off the Wild Shore, each with a crew of 42-45 pirates: Stillwater (45) and Keelhaul (46) on the nearer decks, Fleet Master Firallon (48) on the flagship. At 42 this is a fight for a group or for the end of the guide; clear each deck first if you go. Cortello's scroll lies on the wreck by the shore.
  kill 2550 quest 608 optional        -- Captain Stillwater
  kill 2548 quest 608 optional        -- Captain Keelhaul
  kill 2546 quest 608 optional        -- Fleet Master Firallon
  collect 4056                        -- Cortello's Riddle
  accept 624                          -- for the Swamp of Sorrows later

step Booty Bay
  turnin 608 optional                 -- Fleet Master Seahorn

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- North of the bay

step Naga Explorers
  tip The naga comb the beaches north of the Bloodsail camp; they drop the reeds.
  collect 4029 quest 617              -- Akiris Reed

step Gorilla hills
  tip Ride inland to the Mistvale gorilla hills. Elder Mistvale Gorillas drop the giblets; Witch Doctor Unbagwa sits among them.
  collect 3919 quest 606              -- Mistvale Giblets
  accept 349                          -- Witch Doctor Unbagwa
  collect 2799 quest 349              -- Gorilla Fang

step Unbagwa's ritual
  tip Hand in the fangs and stay: three waves of gorillas come, Mokk the Savage last. Fight at full health.
  turnin 349                          -- Witch Doctor Unbagwa
  collect 2797 quest 348              -- Heart of Mokk

step Booty Bay
  tip Ride back down to town; Shaky stands at the tunnel mouth.
  turnin 606                          -- "Shaky" Phillipe
  accept 607
  turnin 607                          -- "Sea Wolf" MacKinley
  accept 609
  turnin 348                          -- Fin Fizracket
  turnin 617                          -- Privateer Bloads
  accept 623                          -- for Privateer Groy in Theramore: keep it

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The jungle

step Maury and Jon-Jon
  tip Ride north to the hills west of the road. Maury "Club Foot" Wilkins and Jon-Jon the Crow stand together just north of Zanzil's village.
  collect 3924 quest 609              -- Maury's Clubbed Foot
  collect 3925 quest 609              -- Jon-Jon's Golden Spyglass

step Zanzil's village
  tip Every Zanzil follower can drop the mixture; Chucky "Ten Thumbs" walks the south of the camp.
  collect 4016 quest 621              -- Zanzil's Mixture
  collect 3926 quest 609              -- Chucky's Huge Ring

step Crystalvein Mine
  tip Follow the road north-east to the Venture Co. camp at the Crystalvein Mine; the miners, surveyors and foremen drop the crystals.
  collect 3917 quest 600              -- Singing Blue Crystal

step Skullsplitter ruins
  tip The Skullsplitter trolls hold the ruins just east of the mine; any of them can drop tusks, their panthers always do.
  collect 1524 quest 209              -- Skullsplitter Tusk

step Cold Eye Basilisks
  tip The Cold Eye Basilisks lie on the rocks west of the mine.
  collect 2476 quest 212              -- Chilled Basilisk Haunch

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The far north

step The north-west coast
  tip Ride north-west from the mine to the bay on the north-west coast. The Giant Clams lie on its floor and hold the pearls; Gazban swims among them and drops the Stone of the Tides.
  collect 4611 quest 705              -- Blue Pearl
  collect 4034 quest 611              -- Stone of the Tides

step Rebel Camp
  tip Ride north-east past Nesingwary's camp and follow the road north to the camp at the top of the vale. On the way, an Arbor Tarantula crawls in the jungle south-east of Nesingwary's camp: catch one with the Entomology Starter Kit, then tick it off.
  kill 217588                         -- Arbor Tarantula: catch it, for My Little Friends
  turnin 622                          -- Corporal Kaleb

step Booty Bay
  hearth "Booty Bay"
  turnin 611                          -- Baron Revilgaz
  turnin 609                          -- "Sea Wolf" MacKinley
  note MacKinley's next task sends you after elite ogres: skip it.
  turnin 600                          -- Crank Fizzlebub
  turnin 621
  note Crank's next Zanzil errand starts in Thousand Needles: skip it.
  turnin 209                          -- Kebok

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Stormwind

step Stormwind
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Angus Stern cooks in the Blue Recluse; Brohann Caskbelly is in the Dwarven District.
  fly "Stormwind"
  sethome "Stormwind City"
  turnin 212                          -- Angus Stern
  accept 1271
  turnin 1271
  accept 1477                         -- High Sorcerer Andromath: for Nethergarde Keep, keep it
  accept 1363                         -- Mazen Mac'Nadir
  turnin 1363                         -- Acolyte Dellis
  accept 1364
  accept 1448                         -- Brohann Caskbelly
  turnin 542                          -- Milton Sheaf, the Royal Library in Stormwind Keep
  train class only Warrior,Paladin,Hunter,Rogue,Priest,Mage,Warlock,Druid

step Riding at 40
  only Human
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip At 40 with 100 gold you can learn to ride, and learning it gives you a mount. Randal Hunter teaches Humans at Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest, beside Katie Hunter's horses. Forever may let any race learn from any riding trainer (unconfirmed). Collectibles, Mounts · Level 40 lists every colour.
  train 4732 optional                 -- Randal Hunter
  vendor 384 optional                 -- Katie Hunter: other colours, 20g

step Riding at 40
  only Skyborne
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip At 40 with 100 gold you can learn to ride, and learning it gives you a mount. No Skyborne riding trainer is known; the Forever client files Galestrider Riding under the one Riding skill, so Randal Hunter at Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn Forest, the nearest trainer to Stormwind, should teach it (unconfirmed). The Galestriders are sold by Genn Fairweather in Valanaar on Zephras Isle; Collectibles, Mounts · Level 40 lists them.
  train 4732 optional                 -- Randal Hunter
  note "Galestriders: Genn Fairweather, in Valanaar on Zephras Isle."

step Riding at 40
  only NightElf
  zone Darnassus
  tip At 40 with 100 gold you can learn to ride, and learning it gives you a mount. Jartsam teaches Night Elves in Darnassus, beside Lelanai's sabers: the boat from Stormwind Harbor to Auberdine, then the flight to Rut'theran Village. Forever may let any race learn from any riding trainer (unconfirmed), such as Randal Hunter at Eastvale Logging Camp in Elwynn Forest. Collectibles, Mounts · Level 40 lists every colour.
  train 4753 optional                 -- Jartsam
  vendor 4730 optional                -- Lelanai: other colours, 20g

step Paladin: The Tome of Nobility
  only Paladin
  zone Stormwind City
  accept 1661                         -- Duthorian Rall, in the Cathedral of Light
  turnin 1661

step Warlock: Summon Felsteed
  only Warlock
  accept 4488                         -- Demisette Cloyce, in the Slaughtered Lamb: Strahad Farsan in Ratchet takes it at the end of the next guide

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Swamp of Sorrows

step Watcher Biggs
  zone Swamp of Sorrows
  tip Fly to Darkshire and ride east through Deadwind Pass into the Swamp of Sorrows; Watcher Biggs stands by the road just past the border.
  fly "Darkshire"
  accept 1398

step A Soggy Scroll
  tip The scroll lies in the marsh north of Biggs. The Swampwalkers north of it can drop Khadgar's essays.
  turnin 624
  note The riddle's next scroll lies in western Dustwallow: skip it.
  collect 6065 quest 1364             -- Khadgar's Essays on Dimensional Convergence

step The sunken temple
  tip Ride east; the Tangled Horrors along the way also drop the essays. Search the edge of the Pool of Tears, where the temple's ruins break the water.
  collect 6065 quest 1364             -- Khadgar's Essays on Dimensional Convergence
  complete 1448 @70.2,45.2

step Misty Reed Strand
  tip The driftwood washes up along the eastern shore.
  collect 6146 quest 1398             -- Sundried Driftwood

step Watcher Biggs
  tip Ride back west along the road; Amaryllis Webb stands a short way north of Biggs.
  turnin 1398
  accept 1425                         -- for Nethergarde Keep: keep it
  turnin 93176                        -- Amaryllis Webb: My Little Friends, from 30-40/05-arathi-highlands

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Stormwind and Ironforge

step Stormwind
  zone Stormwind City
  hearth "Stormwind City"
  turnin 1448                         -- Brohann Caskbelly
  accept 1449                         -- for Falstad Wildhammer at Aerie Peak: keep it

step Ironforge
  zone Ironforge
  tip Take the Deeprun Tram from the Dwarven District. Roetten is in the Reclaimers' hall by the Hall of Explorers, Prospector Stormpike in the hall itself, Gerrig Bonegrip in the Forlorn Cavern. The next guide flies on to Thelsamar.
  turnin 1467                         -- Roetten Stonehammer
  accept 707                          -- Prospector Stormpike: for Prospector Ironband in Loch Modan, keep it
  turnin 727                          -- Gerrig Bonegrip
  train class only Shaman             -- Stormwind has no shaman trainer

step Riding at 40
  only Dwarf
  zone Dun Morogh
  tip At 40 with 100 gold you can learn to ride, and learning it gives you a mount. Ultham Ironhorn teaches Dwarves at Amberstill Ranch, east of Kharanos on the road to Loch Modan, beside Veron Amberstill's rams. Forever may let any race learn from any riding trainer (unconfirmed). Collectibles, Mounts · Level 40 lists every colour.
  train 4772 optional                 -- Ultham Ironhorn
  vendor 1261 optional                -- Veron Amberstill: other colours, 20g

step Riding at 40
  only Gnome
  zone Dun Morogh
  tip At 40 with 100 gold you can learn to ride, and learning it gives you a mount. Binjy Featherwhistle teaches Gnomes at Steelgrill's Depot, just east of Kharanos, beside Milli Featherwhistle's mechanostriders. Forever may let any race learn from any riding trainer (unconfirmed). Collectibles, Mounts · Level 40 lists every colour.
  train 7954 optional                 -- Binjy Featherwhistle
  vendor 7955 optional                -- Milli Featherwhistle: other colours, 20g
